🔥 VERY IMPORTANT Example (loop trap)
Interviewers LOVE this.
❌ Wrong output
for(var i=0;i<3;i++){
  setTimeout(function(){
    console.log(i);
  },1000);
}
Output:
3
3
3

WHY?
Because:
var is function-scoped
one shared i
closure captures same variable
✅ Fix using let
for(let i=0;i<3;i++){
  setTimeout(()=>{
    console.log(i);
  },1000);
}
Output:
0 1 2

Because let creates new binding each loop.
Huge interview classic.
💼 Real-World Uses of Closures
✅ 1. Data hiding / private variables
function bank(){
  let balance = 1000;
  return {
    getBalance: () => balance,
    deposit: (x) => balance += x
  };
}
Now:

const acc = bank();
acc.deposit(500);
console.log(acc.getBalance());
Nobody can access balance directly.
Privacy via closure.

✅ 2. Function factories
function multiply(x){
  return function(y){
    return x*y;
  }
}
const double = multiply(2);
console.log(double(5));
✅ 3. Currying
Closures power currying.

Interviewers like hearing this.
⚠️ IMPORTANT RULES ABOUT CLOSURES
🚨 Rule 1
Closures capture VARIABLES, not values.
🚨 Rule 2
Closures can cause memory leaks if large objects are captured.
🚨 Rule 3
Every function in JS automatically forms a closure.
Even if you don't explicitly use it.
This is a killer interview insight.
